# Pre-launch hosted data protection

Sample cleanup is complete. The hosted/client target is protected even while pre-launch; incoming real data is not disposable. Retained test work/accounts do not authorize fixtures or automated tests there.

- Four retained identities are explicitly protected: Matt Duffill TEST ACCOUNT, Testsuite Admin, Testsuite Manager and Testsuite Employee. Do not delete, disable or reset them through development tooling.
- Managed fixtures, plans, cleanup, test-user setup and automated suites require the verified dedicated development target. Production confirmations and old project allowlists cannot override the guard.
- The blanket SAMPLE DATA CRITICAL exemption is retired for hosted work. Apply proportionate safeguards to actual data/security risk; use CRITICAL where the applicable workflow requires it. Isolated development work can use FAST, STANDARD or GUARDED as appropriate.
- Keep ordinary migration safety: approved `pg` pattern, no secret exposure, `db:validate` after rename/drop and explicit authorization before destructive schema/data changes.
- Parent owns hosted migration approval/application, NAS provisioning and private environment separation. Local isolated checks do not prove operational readiness.

See `docs/guides/SAMPLE_DATA_PHASE.md` and `docs/guides/LOCAL_DEVELOPMENT.md`.
